Consider the code:

```java
interface Animal {
  void makeSound();
  void move();
}
interface Pet {
  void play();
}
class Dog implements Animal, Pet {
  public void makeSound() { System.out.println("Woof!"); }
  public void play() { System.out.println("Playing fetch"); }
}
public class Test {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Dog dog = new Dog();
    Animal animal = dog;
    Pet pet = dog;
    animal.makeSound();
    pet.play();
  }
}
```

